file).","status":"confirmed"}},{"detail":"The PR replaces one expression in the remover: `find ~/.config/omarchy/themes -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -type d ! -xtype l -printf '%f\\n'`. It listed every non-symlink directory directly under the folder, dot-directories included; it did not descend into a themes folder that is itself a symlink (find -P with -mindepth 1), and a missing folder gave an error on stderr and no names. The helper's glob keeps the same set minus dot-directories. Pinned by the twelve harness and test homes (compared on Linux, per the correction): dot-directories (dotted, hidden, mixed: intended change), symlinked theme (linked), symlinked folder (folded), missing folder, stray file (filed), real directories (copied, cloned, worktree, dashed: identical). Not pinned by any input, so not established: an unreadable themes folder and a theme name containing a newline. The helper alone lists nothing for the first (exit 1) and prints the second as two lines, which the remover would split into two picker entries; old find's '%f\\n' splits it the same way by reading, but no base run covers either. Opinion: both are edge cases with no removal risk (the remover refuses names it cannot find).","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-theme-remove","kind":"file","line":9},{"id":"bin/omarchy-theme-removable","kind":"file","line":15},{"id":"bin/omarchy-theme-removable","kind":"file","line":16},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-guards-test.sh","kind":"test"},{"id":"SW-REQ-261003-390Z","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"Removed-behaviour inventory (by reading; bash is outside the engine's inventory): the old find and what pins each of its behaviours","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["bin/omarchy-theme-remove"],"scenario":"with ~/.config/omarchy/themes symlinked into a dotfiles repo holding theme mine, run omarchy theme remove mine: the theme is removed from the dotfiles repo although the menu offers nothing there"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The helper lists nothing when ~/.config/omarchy/themes is itself a symlink, so the menu offers no theme there. `omarchy theme remove <name>` from a terminal takes the name as given and is unchanged by this PR, so it can still remove a theme directory inside a symlinked folder, which lives in the user's dotfiles. That predates the PR (the PR says the CLI is unchanged); whether the CLI should follow the helper is a separate question.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-theme-remove","kind":"file","line":19},{"id":"bin/omarchy-theme-removable","kind":"file","line":13},{"id":"SW-REQ-261003-390Z","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: should the terminal command also refuse a symlinked themes folder?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"omarchy theme remove through a symlinked themes folder\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent (disclosure effects_unavailable, informs): the analyzer covers C/C++ only, so call-path statements here come from reading the code. The PR's test and the behaviour harness run the real helper, remover and guard batch.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"bin/omarchy-theme-remove","kind":"file","line":9}],"severity":"info","title":"Analysis bounds: no change-effects analysis for bash","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc:remove.theme","shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:mergeMenuSources"],"scenario":"with a user menu file that sets only a label for remove.theme and an empty themes folder, open the menu: does Remove still list Theme (the default row's when: lost in the merge)?"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Per the open known issue KI-MENU-MERGE-OVERRIDE-WIPES-DEFAULTS (pre-existing, not this PR's), a user entry for a row, even a label-only one, is normalized before the merge and overwrites the default row's when: with an empty value. A user who customized remove.theme would then keep the old unguarded row. The fixed known issue's own scope note for this PR says a user override replaces the whole row, guard included. This affects every guarded row; a test would settle it for this one.","refs":[{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-MERGE-OVERRIDE-WIPES-DEFAULTS.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-REMOVE-THEME-NO-THEMES.yaml","kind":"file","line":27},{"id":"default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc","kind":"file","line":297},{"id":"SW-REQ-261003-390Z","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: does a user menu that overrides remove.theme drop the new guard?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"A label-only user override of remove.theme over an empty themes folder\".","status":"needs_test"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:e43d1f8e50553e88c6ea45361ff0de258a995f92cdf0f9ddc829730539ebdcf3","packageIdentity":"epkg-52c7daff6d1b26470ef14025224bc6417163f9080f03b5a37cacb9e9631f1d5e","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"A small change: one new 21-line helper, one changed line in the remover and one guard on the row, pinned by a twelve-home test. Medium, not low, because the package's behaviour-diff record does not compare the guard (see the correction): the Linux record carries 8 intended compatibility changes a human must approve, the scripts have no engine-measured code MC/DC, and the half-second stale-answer window and the user-override case are not measured. Not merge approval."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":7,"rationale":"Measures the stale-answer window for this row in a running shell.","refs":[{"id":"default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc","kind":"file","line":297},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-guards-test.sh","kind":"file","line":441}],"title":"Open Remove right after removing the last extra theme"},{"forClaim":10,"rationale":"Pins what the terminal command does where the menu offers nothing.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-theme-remove","kind":"file","line":19}],"title":"omarchy theme remove through a symlinked themes folder"},{"forClaim":12,"rationale":"Shows whether the new when: survives the user-menu merge, or whether the open merge known issue brings the unguarded row back.","refs":[{"id":"default/omarchy/omarchy-menu.jsonc","kind":"file","line":297},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-MERGE-OVERRIDE-WIPES-DEFAULTS.yaml","kind":"file","line":1}],"title":"A label-only user override of remove.theme over an empty themes folder"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** omacom/omarchy#14153 (head 9a160c1f) fixes #14150: on a machine with only the bundled themes, Remove > Theme ran a remover with nothing to offer and only closed the menu. The upstream change adds omarchy-theme-removable, which lists the themes the remover can remove (directories that are not symlinks or dot-directories, nothing in a symlinked folder) and exits nonzero when there are none; the row asks it as its when:, and the remover reads its list from it. Evaluated as ab847cc2 on baseline 1e433732 (upstream quattro 035ce29f; upstream change applied as cb2d235e, unchanged); the proof work on top (requirement SW-REQ-261003-390Z, known issue, harness and 12 inputs, trace reviews) changes no product line.\n\n**Correction.** The package's behaviour-diff record says compatible, no differences (225 inputs). That record is wrong for this PR: it was produced on macOS, where the Remove > Theme inputs need GNU find and bash 4+ and print UNAVAILABLE on both sides, so they compare equal. The same run on Linux records 8 intended differences (the same 8 ids as the previous evaluation, all against 390Z): the row is hidden for an empty, missing, symlink-only, file-only, dot-only or symlinked themes folder, where the remover has nothing to offer, and next to a real theme the picker no longer offers .git. Each needs a human reviewer's approval. A re-evaluation with the Linux record follows.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** Audit run 0 errors, 0 warnings. Tests ingested and current: 68/68 passed; all 29 changed requirements observed_pass; 25 obligation cells observed_pass, 29 not_linked, 5 suppressed by recorded reasons (not evidence). The scripts are not code-MC/DC targets (0 changed decisions measured).\n\n**Questions for a human.** Approve or reject each of the 8 differences. The first open of a session, or right after the last theme goes away, can show the row for about half a second (as for every guarded row). Does a user override of remove.theme drop the guard (open merge known issue)? Should the terminal command refuse a symlinked folder (unchanged)?\n\n**Traceability.** All 18 changed files map; no spec-gap candidate; no suspect link.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** coverage_unmeasured, checks_skipped and effects_unavailable inform only.\n\nThe package states readiness ready, next decision human_judgement (acceptance), maintainer authority. This review is advisory; nothing here is an approval."}
